he's great to see everybody again first  and foremost because again we spent a  lot of time with them but great to hear  their stories great to hear where they  are how things I had no idea that Damien  and Jie were back together dating I mean  it's that's that's awesome that Lauren  and Cameron got a dog or you know that  Jessica's and Kelly have had so much  self-reflection and it's just it was  really cool we asked them all to come  and that was on their choice to come  back and so to have these 10 incredible  individuals coming back for this show to  kind of speak their mind and say their  piece and and unite on this front of  what love is blind was really beautiful  and when we asked all of them would you  do it again knowing what you know now  knowing what ever you know perception is  reality in this world knowing what you  know now knowing how the show came out  knowing the hurt or the passion that you  found would you do it again all ten of  them said yes yes here you will choose  someone to marry without ever seeing  will you be my wife we didn't know if  there'd be a single proposal much less  you know six proposals and and I think  what we saw and saw very quickly were  these very genuine connections that  people were making you know sight unseen  just talking through a wall and  especially from my perspective because I  was dealing with more of the guys is  that seeing these grown men you know  like I don't to say crumbled but like I  mean really they became very unafraid to  show their emotion and be vulnerable and  I think they all would tell you they  learned a lot about themselves about  life about love from being a part of  this experiment if you will so I was  really cool for us to kind of watch all  that you know from the sidelines and be  a part of it we did get nervous like I  remember we got nervous we're like  because nobody made anybody propose let  me make that very clear this was all on  their own but once they did propose  we're like now we're gonna document all  the way to the altar and at that point  you can walk away or you can say I do  but are you gonna walk away from someone  you fell in love with and felt the need  to propose to and so I think even the  the lovers I'm gonna call them lovers  not contestants cuz that seems weird the  lovers  we're like there's no way I'm gonna find  my my partner my fiancee and then within  three days some of them six days some of  them eight days they're like oh my gosh  I don't want to lose this person and I  want I want to continue this journey  with this  and I want to marry this person that's  all real and it's really beautiful to be  part of there are definitely a lot of  moments really whoa like when we were  watching it you know I think one that's  that's that's glaring is the Carlton  diamond relationship and for us to be a  part of that on the other side and you  know you obviously didn't see a lot of  it we actually talked to every single  one of them daily so after every date we  were there in the halls talking with  them and then we would go into the men's  quarters in the women's quarters and we  would actually sit down on the couch and  have conversations like how are you  feeling what's going on not that we know  the way to do marriage of relationships  we're just a sounding board of like the  old married couple like talk to me talk  to me as somebody who's not in the pod  with you or talk to me another woman  who's not competing to find this other  guy what's going on in your mind and so  to have watch to know Carlton in to know  Diamond and to see how great they were  individually and then when they finally  came together but then have this other  layer you watched his journey of  struggling to tell her but then you also  watch the journey of her struggling to  understand it and all very quickly she's  like you've looked lived with this your  entire life and then in fact lived with  it the entire tell me that they were  courting she's like I've had one night  I've one night to kind of digest it so I  think that the beautiful thing that the  show is allowed is for everyone to  hopefully have a takeaway of how to  better communicate with other people and  empathy and have an understanding that  you never know what someone else is  going through and also not to ever take  that for granted when somebody's there  for you and wants to open up and be  vulnerable and the power of  vulnerability this is why I don't deal  with it's like you  you all call me my face I don't do what  women like you yeah yo people are coming  at her from one side which I completely  get on their end but they're getting a  piece of the puzzle so I think for her  it was just about person-to-person  understanding like something that wasn't  told to me and and trying to - Carlton's  point trying to understand it in a way  where cameras or social media aren't  involved and they are and so I think for  them it was humbling and I thought was  beautiful about today was them both  being willing to acknowledge and  recognize that they probably could have  handled it a little better you know from  both sides and and coming to some kind  of resolution that you know that you  know that was satisfactory to both of  them because you look from our  perspective when you're a part of these  people's day every week we were kind of  rooting for everybody I mean you want to  see everyone figure this out and it was  you know it kind of sucked to be honest  the way that turned out so it was nice  today to see some resolution to a couple  of the situations but especially that  way yeah  [Music]

